@format 1
@id processing.source-output-collision
@title Handle source and output path collision
@area 5. Processing and FFmpeg
@entry input
@summary Trace work creation and collision handling when an output path can equal one of its source paths, including the destructive failure paths under Rename existing and Overwrite.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related processing.run-job, queue.create-edit-work, queue.create-convert-work, queue.create-audio-work, queue.create-split-work, queue.create-merge-work
@tag collision
@tag overwrite

@alias edit = Cadroue.Application.LEdit
@alias convert = Cadroue.Application.LConvert
@alias audio = Cadroue.Application.LAudio
@alias split = Cadroue.Application.LSplit
@alias merge = Cadroue.Application.LMerge
@alias job = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LJob
@alias encode = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LEncode

[input] Work output path is formed <input>
- Avoid an exact source/output path match by appending an edit suffix for Edit work @ edit.LEditNameCreate(...)
- Avoid an exact source/output path match by appending a convert suffix for Convert work @ convert.LConvertNameCreate(...)
- Avoid an exact source/output path match by appending an audio suffix for Audio work @ audio.LAudioNameCreate(...)
- Create Split names with within-batch uniqueness but without a full-path comparison against the source @ split.LSplitNameCreate(...)
- Create Merge names with within-batch uniqueness but without comparison against every merge source @ merge.LMergeNameCreate(...)
> equality

[equality] Does a work item retain equal source and output paths? <decision>
? "Paths differ" > normal
? "Output equals a source path" > validate

[validate] Validate stored work independently <process>
- Confirm that source files exist and that the output path is non-empty without rejecting source/output equality @ job.LJobValidate(...)
> policy

[policy] Apply selected collision policy <decision>
- Detect that the target already exists because it is also a source file @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
? "Rename output" > rename-output
? "Rename existing" > rename-existing
? "Overwrite" > overwrite

[rename-output] Move output to a free path <process>
- Resolve a free output name and update the work item's output path @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
> normal

[rename-existing] Move the existing source away <error>
- Rename the existing target file while leaving the work item's source path unchanged @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
- Build the later FFmpeg command with the now-missing original source path @ encode.LEncodeArgumentBuild(...)
> broken

[overwrite] Keep identical input and output <error>
- Leave the equal source and output paths unchanged under Overwrite @ job.LJobCollisionApply(...)
- Build an FFmpeg command with overwrite enabled and the same path as input and output @ encode.LEncodeHeaderAppend(...)
> broken

[normal] Continue with distinct paths <output>
= FFmpeg receives separate source and output paths.

[broken] Processing chain fails <output>
= The job reaches FFmpeg with either a missing source path or the same file as input and output, so normal completion and relay cannot proceed.
